# Editors / tooling
.idea
.vs
__pycache__/
*.user
*.suo

# Build output. `bin` and `obj` cover the normal .NET locations, including
# tests/unwrap/bin. The patterns below catch compiled output that lands anywhere
# else - a copy taken by hand, a stray deploy, a rollback saved during a session.
bin
obj
TestResults/
*.pdb
*.exe
*.nupkg
*.dll

# ...but the FROZEN BUILD ARTIFACTS are deliberate and tracked, so they are
# exempted rather than needing `git add -f` every time one is taken.
#
# Read the negation as a rule about intent: a dll whose name carries the commit
# and the md5 is EVIDENCE - COORDINATION.md cites several of them by filename,
# and the whole point of freezing a binary is being able to say which one a
# measurement came from. A dll anywhere else is detritus. The pattern is what
# tells those two apart, so do not "simplify" it away.
#
# It matches direct children of artifacts/ only, which is why a hand-taken copy
# in artifacts/rollback/ stays ignored.
!artifacts/Framesaver-*.dll

# Rollback copies taken before a deploy. Useful on disk, not history.
artifacts/rollback/
